A||||5||ICQ196344||tach & speedometer mod
Z||000000||ICQ196344||05-25-99||02:26 PM||||I am looking for someone with electronic expertise to confirm the steps I am about to take to modify the tach and speedometer on my '84 Fiero V-8.To change the tach I to read the V-8 engine properly I will replace the capacitor on the tach circiut board with one rated at.0064uf. To increase the speedometer from 85 MPH to 120 MPH max reading I plan on replacing the crystal on the speedometer circiut board with a 4.43 MHz crystal.I hope someone can confirm before I begin. 
Z||000001||theogre||05-25-99||08:19 PM||||you are better off just getting a 120 speedo, or using one of the digital dash products like the one Cliff makes. I beleive he can program that tach to do about anything you want. There are a few people with 120 speedo's for sale. look around. what's another 100$ if you are going to that much trouble already.<p>As for changing the tach value,,,, if it's a v6 tach it's worth the trouble. a 4 cyl tach isn't it just doesn't read high enough.
Z||000002||ezsurf||05-25-99||09:48 PM||||ICQ196344,<br>The "Big Fiero Parts Book" confirms the capacitor rating for the V-8 tach at .0064uF.  Couldn't tell you about the Mhz of the crystal.  Although, it sounds like your information is accurate. 
Z||000003||Cliff Pennock||05-26-99||12:38 AM||||Ezsurf, what's the cap value for a V6? I can't seem to find that anywhere.<br>
Z||000004||Cliff Pennock||05-26-99||12:41 AM||||ICQ196344, I meant that you should contact me on that ICQ number, not use it as a username! LOL!
Z||000005||ezsurf||05-26-99||06:39 AM||||Cliff,<br>The book lists the capacitor value for the V-6 as .0082uF.  The value for the 4 cylinder is .01uF. (uF = micro Farads).
